1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
In the Kolo 2026.0 version, we have made several major updates to the depth of field part, including the hardware picture based on the fabric attribute, the depth pressure picture display effect switch, and the depth of field attribute will be stored in the project file, and so on.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The following will be carefully introduced to you. First is the hardware picture based on the fabric attribute. In the past, some users may feel that there is a difference between the visual information displayed on the hardware picture and the actual results.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Now we have improved this. By considering the physical characteristics of each type of fabric, it is easier and more intuitive to check the stretch of the fabric.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I will provide a detailed explanation of this through a visual document. Two types of fabrics were applied in the visual document. The middle panel was applied with a single cloth, and the side was applied with a needle fabric.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Now let's activate the hardware picture.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
In the vertical menu bar of the 3D window, you will see a depth chart icon. You can see the hardware picture, hardware picture, cloth picture, and depth pressure picture.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
We click on the hardware picture icon to activate it. After activating the hardware picture, you will see the hardware picture window at the top of the 2D window.

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Before adjusting the detailed properties of the hardware picture, you need to set the first option to activate it in the depth attribute.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
But in this version, the window will immediately display after activating the hardware picture. It is more convenient to adjust.

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
You can also check the new features in the hardware picture.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Now I will explain the difference between the two modes.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
First, let's look at the general mode.

13
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
As before, the standard value of all fabrics is absolutely the same.

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The general mode is used to objectively check the physical deformation of the fabric itself.

15
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
There is no need to consider the characteristics of the fabric itself.

16
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The standard value of the fixed fabric can be adjusted freely and can be verified by dividing it into 8 segments.

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
When the user inputs the largest value, the system will automatically calculate the middle value between the largest and the smallest value, and divide it into 8 segment applications.

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Therefore, if the maximum value is set to 120, all fabrics that are more than the point of deformation will be displayed as red.

19
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Click on any position on the clothing to check the specific hardware value of the point.

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Therefore, the general mode is based on the set ratio operation without considering the specific physical properties of the fabric.

21
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
At this time, I will manually change the maximum hardware value to 150% and simulate it.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You can see that the color will automatically change according to the new range.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Since the upper limit value has increased, the range of red has significantly decreased.

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Change back to 120% again and simulate the same step.

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
In this mode, when the elastic fabric stretches more than 120%, there will be no problem of tightness when wearing.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:40,000
But because its stretch value is above the set standard value, the system will often unconditionally display it as red.

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
As a result, we cannot judge its difference based on the maximum stretch strength of the fabric.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
On the contrary, in the fabric mode, the stretch strength of the fabric is higher.

29
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The standard mode shows the maximum stretch strength of the fabric.

30
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Based on the stretch strength calculated by the fabric, it represents the stretch strength of the fabric that cannot continue to stretch when the outer force is increased.

31
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
In this way, you can check the unity of the fabric according to the maximum stretch strength of each fabric itself to ensure that the characteristics of the fabric are accurately reflected.

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The state of the body is also clearer.

33
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Now let's choose the fabric mode.

34
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Similar to the general mode, the range of visualization is to divide the space between the 100% standard value and the stretch limit of each fabric into 8 segments.

35
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:20,000
The core difference between the 8 segments and the general mode is that there is a stretch limit area.

36
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Here, the system will automatically calculate and apply the limit range according to the unique stretch characteristics of each fabric.

37
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
This stretch limit represents a zero-sum value.

38
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:38,000
In other words, you can understand it as a turning point that is not determined as too tight in the actual wear.

39
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
For example, as you can see,

40
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:52,000
the stretch limit value of the fabric is 138% in the front, 148% in the back, 146% and 157% in the front.

41
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The stretch limit value of the denim fabric is 103% in the front, 102% in the back, and 112% in the back.

42
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Since the stretch value of each fabric is different, the simulation results are also different from the general standard.

43
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Let's run the simulation and check the results.

44
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Now you can see that it is different from the general mode.

45
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Now you can see that it is different from the general mode.

46
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
The simulation results are different from the general mode.

47
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
The elasticity of the denim fabric used in the chest area is less, and it has stretched to the limit.

48
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Therefore, the area will display a tight state with a straight red bar.

49
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
In contrast, the fabric of high elasticity needle needs to be stretched more to reach its limit.

50
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Therefore, in the clothes, it has not stretched to the limit, which shows a straight blue bar that means that it is in a state where it is loose and not tight.

51
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,000
But if you modify its physical properties after fabric application, the hardware photo will not apply these modifications in real time.

52
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Therefore, it must be refreshed once.

53
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,800
For example, if you replace the fabric with a different fabric or adjust its physical properties,

54
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:52,600
you can press the refresh button on the top right corner of the fabric to update it with the stretch value of the changed fabric.

55
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:55,600
After opening the simulation, check the hard change of the new fabric,

56
00:04:55,600 --> 00:05:03,899
because the stretch and limit value of this fabric are larger, so most areas are displayed as blue.

57
00:05:03,899 --> 00:05:07,899
You can also manually change the stretch limit.

58
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Press this button to restore the original value.

59
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
To refresh the stretch value of all fabrics, please press the refresh button at the top.

60
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Below is the display type modifier.

61
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Allow you to set the hard change distribution state to the style you like.

62
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
